                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67f4165c-ca3e-3b0b-8a62-94df589417c7",
                        "entry_id": "1fa36743-c857-31f0-b677-2b630971af55",
                        "glosses": [
                            "спец. точный переносной часовой механизм с балансиром, используемый при астрономических и геодезических наблюдениях, а также в морском деле"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4028cfd7-e651-4cdd-8251-150ba8cfb475",
                                "sense_id": "67f4165c-ca3e-3b0b-8a62-94df589417c7",
                                "text": ".. долгота, по хронометрам определённая после полудня, хотя и при весьма неверном горизонте, показала прямое расстояние до берега в 62 милях .."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6b084ce7-0965-3ec3-bd2f-c357ea51a8c1",
                        "entry_id": "1fa36743-c857-31f0-b677-2b630971af55",
                        "glosses": [
                            "механические часы с особо точным ходом"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46252bab-9dde-44ab-aa68-54ab2969db4d",
                                "sense_id": "6b084ce7-0965-3ec3-bd2f-c357ea51a8c1",
                                "text": "Он вынул из кармана великолепный хронометр, неизвестно для чего заставил его прозвонить, затем открыл крышку, взглянул на циферблат .."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ee21c95c-4ad0-4aad-9929-54f0b0ab5c61",
                        "source_entry_id": "1fa36743-c857-31f0-b677-2b630971af55",
                        "target_lang_word": "chronometer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chronometer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "becf2e6f-d75d-3d6f-b214-1085c248e58f",
                                        "entry_id": "cb8615c3-5ef2-3fe5-acd8-73758e3e0b68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device for measuring time, particularly a precision mechanism for measuring time of day."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fbdbb6b-bd9e-4c16-a17f-20003c411b47",
                                                "sense_id": "becf2e6f-d75d-3d6f-b214-1085c248e58f",
                                                "text": "A wristwatch costs $20. A chronometer costs $20,000."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61fdaa44-96ab-4944-9476-d9de022b786b",
                                                "sense_id": "becf2e6f-d75d-3d6f-b214-1085c248e58f",
                                                "text": "The balances of all moveable time-keepers, the chronometer excepted, are prevented from vibrating beyond the proper arc by what is called bankings. The inferior escapements are very easily banked; a pin fixed in the balance, coming in contact with one or two studs, is sufficient for that purpose. […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d03d58b-c856-42b7-b91d-37f03a357dbf",
                                                "sense_id": "becf2e6f-d75d-3d6f-b214-1085c248e58f",
                                                "text": "The stock-in-trade of this old gentleman comprised chronometers, barometers, telescopes, compasses, charts, maps, sextants, quadrants, and specimens of every kind of instrument used in the working of a ship's course, or the keeping of a ship's reckoning, or the prosecuting of a ship's discoveries."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e80e4038-e03f-4114-baf3-e60eed1b0801",
                                                "sense_id": "becf2e6f-d75d-3d6f-b214-1085c248e58f",
                                                "text": "The sailors sail by chronometers that do not lose two or three seconds in a year, ever since [Isaac] Newton explained to Parliament that the way to improve navigation was to get good watches, and to offer public premiums for a better time-keeper than any then in use."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6378b29-5ff2-4288-bde6-458210652b16",
                        "source_entry_id": "1fa36743-c857-31f0-b677-2b630971af55",
